    "category": "Herd immunity threshold",
    "stem": "A community has 70% of its population immune to a disease. The disease still spreads, slowly. What is the most likely explanation?",
    "options": {
      "A": "The disease has mutated to a new variant the immune population can't handle.",
      "B": "70% is below the herd immunity threshold for this disease, so transmission chains still happen between unimmune people.",
      "C": "Herd immunity requires 100% coverage to work at all.",
      "D": "Vaccines only work for two weeks after administration."
    },
    "correct": "B"
  },
